# Allowlist build context (build from repo root): ONLY what games2/Dockerfile
# COPYs. New top-level domains stay out of the context (and off the deploy
# critical path) until the Dockerfile actually bakes them in.
*
!games2
# The music ARCHIVE (every generated take, kept so the maintainer can swap
# one back in) is wiki content, not game content: the engine never requests
# a pool/ bed, and the wiki reads what is not in the image from the repo CDN.
# 97 MB measured 2026-08-22. foley/*/pool stays IN: assigned takes live there
# (thunder__cand07..17) and the engine's take lookup searches it.
games2/composer/music/pool
# The maintainer's hand-drawn SOURCE art (5.6 MB): build INPUTS for the bake
# scripts, which are run offline and commit their output — the Dockerfile
# never invokes them and nothing serves ui-src, so every image carried it for
# nothing. The bakes it produces (client/public/ui2) ship as they always did.
# — games-ui 2026-09-03
games2/client/ui-src
games2/node_modules
games2/client/dist
games2/**/*.tsbuildinfo
games2/.data
!scenery
!characters2
!tiles2
# ...but NOT the tiles2 generator's source sheets. tiles2/<terrain>/raw/ is the
# pre-postprocess output the tiles2 agent keeps so it can re-tune and re-run
# (tiles2/config/tiles2.json: "Raw is always kept"). The GAME never reaches it:
# zero references in any maps2 world.json, in games2 source, or in the wiki's
# build/data. 4,648 files / 34 MB baked into every image for nothing.
tiles2/*/raw
!maps2
!sounds
!music
# The music WAV masters (~61 MB) are the music domain's analysis source-of-truth,
# never fetched by the game: the engine streams ogg/m4a (musicStreamUrl) and the
# /#music viewer streams too. Keep them OUT of the deploy image so every roll is
# ~61 MB lighter. Sounds stay wav (SFX are wav-only in the catalog). Revert this
# line if a music consumer ever needs the master at runtime. — games-audio 2026-07-25
music/**/*.wav
!monsters
!items
# Tiles 3.0 (/tiles) — the 3rd-generation isometric tile system, developed in
# parallel with tiles2, which keeps shipping and is unaffected. Only the reviewable
# output is tracked (tiles/review + config + pipeline, 121 files / 584K); the raw
# candidate sheets in tiles/matrix are gitignored and never enter the context.
# NOTE: this line alone does not put it in the image — games2/Dockerfile also needs
# `COPY tiles/ tiles/`, which is the game agent's file. Asked on the board 2026-08-17.
!tiles
!lore
!wiki
!live
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
*.log
